                <pb facs="0443" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg345"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Choate.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Circular—Telegram.—Paraphrase.]<anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d428-f1"/></seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1900-07-18"><hi rendition="#italic">July 18,
                                1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(In view of request of Viceroys presented to the President yesterday by the
                    Chinese minister that Tientsin be not destroyed, the President has instructed
                    the United States officers in China that nothing but military necessity would
                    justify destruction of city, and hoped that no such necessity might arise.)</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d428-f1" n="2" xml:id="d428-f1-content">
                <p>Also sent to Berlin, Paris, and St. Petersburg.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
